From: "Pluet, LLC" <358065800+pluetllc@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] av1: export the Dolby Vision RPU in HEVC's layout; attach it
 to VideoToolbox frames

Dolby Vision profile 10 (AV1: 10.0, 10.1, 10.4) carries its RPU in ITU-T
T.35 metadata OBUs wrapped in EMDF. The AV1 decoders (native and libdav1d)
parse it into AV_FRAME_DATA_DOVI_METADATA but, unlike the HEVC decoder,
export no AV_FRAME_DATA_DOVI_RPU_BUFFER. Apple's display pipeline takes a
Dolby Vision frame's RPU as the pixel buffer's DolbyVisionRPUData
attachment, in the layout the HEVC decoder exports (the UNSPEC62 NAL payload
after its header: the 0x19 prefix and the RPU, emulation prevention
included), which a Dolby Vision HEVC VideoToolbox session attaches to its
output by itself. VideoToolbox has no Dolby Vision AV1 session, so an AV1
profile 10 frame reached the display as its base layer only.

ff_dovi_attach_rpu_buffer() writes the parsed metadata back out with
ff_dovi_rpu_generate() (FF_DOVI_WRAP_NAL, no metadata compression), from a
DOVIContext the decoder keeps for that alone, checks that FFmpeg's own
parser takes it back (CRC32 included; its refusals are logged at trace
level), and attaches it as AV_FRAME_DATA_DOVI_RPU_BUFFER: an RPU the writer
cannot reproduce (an empty DM v1 block list) is never handed on. Both AV1 decoders call it after attaching the
metadata; a failure is logged at debug level and leaves the frame as it was.
On a VideoToolbox frame the native decoder then hands the RPU to
ff_videotoolbox_attach_dovi_rpu(), which sets it as DolbyVisionRPUData on
the decoded buffer unless it has one. Software-decoded frames get the side
data only: vo_avfoundation's profile 5 path (mpv 0004, region "avf dovi
profile5 rpu") attaches it to a frame without an HDR10/HLG base (10.0) and
leaves 10.1 and 10.4 frames presenting their base layer, as profile 8.

The av1 and libdav1d decoders select dovi_rpuenc, which now selects
dovi_rpudec for that check.

scripts/test_dovi_rpu_layers.sh builds a host libavcodec of the Apple series
and writes back every RPU in libdovi's test assets: each parses to the same
header, mapping, colour metadata and extension blocks (profile 4's colour
metadata excepted, which no AV1 stream carries), and the one the writer
cannot reproduce is refused.

Checked on the host with a profile 10.1 AV1 file encoded by libsvtav1 from a
profile 8.1 HEVC file: every frame carries an RPU dovi_tool parses (CRC32
intact), with the same mapping and the same level 1, 2, 4, 5, 6, 9, 11 and
254 metadata as the source's, in another block order.

